meta {
  name: List Workbook Table Specs (CLI)
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/cli/v1/workbooks/{{workbookId}}/table-specs
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~connectorAccountId: {{connectorAccountId}}
  ~metadataOnly: true
}

docs {
  DEV-13025. Every linked folder's table spec (`schema.json`) and default view
  (`views/default.json`) in the workbook, grouped by connection, read from
  Postgres. `scratchmd` writes them into its local cache instead of copying them
  from git. Each file is `present` (the stored text, verbatim, plus the SHA-256 of
  its UTF-8 bytes), `absent`, or `unreadable`. A connection with no linked folders
  is listed with an empty `dataFolders`.

  - `connectorAccountId` limits the listing to one connection (404 if it isn't in
    the workbook).
  - `metadataOnly=true` leaves out `content` and keeps `sha256`, for change
    detection.

  Read-only.
}
